// W1 AFF (before-evidence, OLD-1V): the between-transition corruption
// SURVIVES a subsequent gate REJECT. Honest commit; init re-seeds appA to
// 999 between transitions; the next transition is correctly REJECTED
// (IAB violated on the seeded value) — but the REJECT restores nothing:
// the seeded 999 REMAINS the committed state. (The mid-transition analogue
// was the 1V F2 demonstration on OLD-1U; this is the same shape BETWEEN
// transitions on the FIXED 1V model.)
init(appA,0,5) , init(appB,0,3) , as(appB) , begin , w(appB,0,2) , wfCheck , gate , init(appA,0,999) , as(appB) , begin , w(appB,0,2) , wfCheck , gate
